repairs.note:
Fix the observed durability race in saveBookmark, keeping the frozen node-web plan unchanged (replan=false). The formal fresh-install run built successfully but lost Desk Lamp after reload: UI data.set happens before awaited IndexedDB put, so a card can appear before the transaction is durable. In a separate diagnostic copy, replacing only saveBookmark to await db.bookmarks.put(bm) BEFORE data.set(bm.id,bm) passed build and all 50 browser checks, including two saved links after reload, real saved-URL navigation target, category refiling after save feedback, category browsing and search. This reused installed dependencies and is diagnostic evidence only, not formal acceptance. Return a single unique replacement of this existing function:
  async function saveBookmark(bm: Bookmark) {
    data.set(bm.id, bm);
    await db.bookmarks.put(bm);
  }
with the identical function containing the two statements in the opposite order. Preserve everything else: default parameters already fixed, source UI and behavior, four render files, package.json, exact LICENSE, metadata attribution and all technical plan steps. Use files={} and one replacement; no full-file rewrite or replanning. Do not claim successful formal verification or publish; Atlas will test this new frozen candidate independently.

source_patch.old:
async function saveBookmark(bm: Bookmark) {
  data.set(bm.id, bm);
  await db.bookmarks.put(bm);
}

source_patch.new:
async function saveBookmark(bm: Bookmark) {
  await db.bookmarks.put(bm);
  data.set(bm.id, bm);
}
